Q1. What is the Decorator Design Pattern?
Why do we need it?

Interview Ready Answer

The Decorator Pattern is a
Structural Design Pattern
that allows us to add new
functionality to an existing object
dynamically (at runtime)
without modifying its original class.

It wraps the existing object
with another object (Decorator)
that adds additional behavior.

------------------------------------------------------------

Why do we need Decorator Pattern?

• Add new functionality at runtime.
• Avoid modifying existing classes.
• Follow Open/Closed Principle (OCP).
• Avoid subclass explosion.
• Improve flexibility and maintainability.

------------------------------------------------------------

What problem does it solve?

Without Decorator,

adding multiple features requires
creating many subclasses.

Decorator allows adding
features dynamically by
wrapping the object.

------------------------------------------------------------

Real-Life Example

Gift Wrapping

Mobile

↓

Gift Paper

↓

Ribbon

↓

Greeting Card

The Mobile remains the same.

Each wrapper adds
a new feature.

------------------------------------------------------------

Software Industry Example

Notification

↓

EmailDecorator

↓

SMSDecorator

↓

WhatsAppDecorator

Each decorator adds
a new notification channel
without modifying
the original Notification class.

