Q2. Difference between Decorator Pattern
and Inheritance

Interview Ready Answer

Inheritance

• Uses extends.
• Adds functionality
  through subclasses.
• Behavior is fixed
  at compile time.
• Can create many subclasses.

------------------------------------------------------------

Decorator Pattern

• Uses object composition.
• Wraps an existing object.
• Adds functionality
  at runtime.
• Avoids subclass explosion.
• More flexible.

------------------------------------------------------------

